# 6️⃣ Implement Stack Using Queue

## 📖 Problem

Implement Stack operations using Queue.

Required operations:

```text
push()
pop()
top()
empty()
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Use one or two queues.

For a single queue:

After inserting an element, rotate the previous elements behind it.

---

### Example

Push:

```text
10
20
30
```

Queue becomes:

```text
30 10 20
```

Front represents the Stack Top.

---

### Complexity

```text
Push → O(n)

Pop  → O(1)
```

---

# 7️⃣ Implement Queue Using Stack

## 📖 Problem

Implement Queue using Stack.

Required operations:

```text
push()
pop()
peek()
empty()
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Use two stacks:

```text
Input Stack

+

Output Stack
```

---

### Example

Enqueue:

```text
10
20
30
```

Input Stack:

```text
30
20
10
```

Transfer to Output Stack:

```text
10
20
30
```

Now the first inserted element is available at the top.

---

### Complexity

With the two-stack approach:

```text
Amortized Time: O(1)
```

